{
  "id": "numeric-stream-skip-grid",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Numeric keys with conditional skips",
  "question": "Do the source no-Fibonacci numeric streams produce complete LP2 outputs above their original English score gate when conditional key skips are permitted?",
  "reader_question": "Can these numeric keys decode pages when key positions may be skipped?",
  "summary": "The 33 fixed numeric streams received 36,300 short screens. Of 322 selected complete-page decodes, none cleared the source \u22125.5 score bar. Known-text controls expose imperfect exact recovery despite passing score gates.",
  "finding": "Unchanged source no-Fibonacci sweep: 36,300 screens at length 50 and beam 60; 322 complete-page confirmations at beam 200; none above \u22125.5. Best complete score \u22126.412430009764881 on LP2-49, \u03c6 digits, subtraction, Atbash and offset 1. All 36,622 scores independently checked; all 322 full paths plus best screen independently reconstructed. Separately labelled post-target audit scores all 56,273 retained terminal candidates; none above \u22125.5, best normalized candidate \u22126.3721459414573545 at the same setting. Original source selections preserved.",
  "reader_finding": "None of the 322 complete-page outputs selected by this numeric-key search cleared its English-score bar. The strongest complete output was on LP2-49.",
  "reader_limit": "Only the listed 33 streams, five key phases, conditional-skip rule and English screen. Rejected short screens were not decoded as complete pages; a high score alone does not establish a reading.",
  "limitations": "The source beam can prefer an alternative over the exact planted reading: 634 of 660 numeric controls recover exactly although all 660 pass both score gates. The full 1,080-cell control receipt includes Atbash duplicates and periodic phase aliases. No complete-search null calibration or general numeric-family exclusion; finite e approximation and historical BBS constructors retained. Cumulative beam ranking differs from normalized gate scoring; the separately labelled terminal-candidate audit preserves that distinction.",
  "next_steps": "Any proposed new key or phase requires frozen input values,matched complete-reading controls and independent verification of a predicted reading.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
